{"id":"sh/mt4fadgj","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":242,"width":1184,"height":97},"text":"The shifts above are in arcseconds. The feature stays at detector pixel (1709, 1364). Three usable stars predict almost the same apparent sky shift for that fixed pixel as the pointing changes. Their own sky positions agree within 0.76″.","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/nudg3ix4","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":355,"width":1184,"height":41},"text":"Adverse mission flags support the check. The feature’s physical cause remains unknown.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
